    <string name="ui_326fa54aae51" formatted="false">"Direct Home-button handling.\n\nFirst enable CleanFrame Home button in TV Accessibility, then turn on Home interception here.\n\nHome opens CleanFrame once on release. Held Home uses the same action. Google stays enabled; Open Google launcher pauses interception."</string>
    <string name="ui_717af1205610" formatted="false">"Read-only package status.\n\nNo commands run from this app. Refresh reads Android again.\n\nKEEP packages must remain unchanged."</string>
    <string name="ui_37e5df95d51f" formatted="false">"Your apps, your order.\n\nChoose an app to open it or add it to Home. Editing this menu does not install or remove an app."</string>
    <string name="ui_f40fc6a77c53" formatted="false">"A photograph. Your apps. Room to breathe.\n\nAll preferences stay on this TV. No advertising, analytics or network access."</string>
    <string name="ui_9d31b32cf353" formatted="false">"On Sharp AQUOS, open the TV menu:\n\nSettings (設定) → Other settings (その他の設定) → Accessibility (ユーザー補助).\n\nAt the bottom, under Services (サービス), turn CleanFrame Home button On.\n\nThen return to CleanFrame → Settings → Home button → Turn on Home interception.\n\nMenu names may differ on other TVs."</string>
    <string name="ui_21e9df992513" formatted="false">"You will be taken to the original Google launcher and Home interception will be turned off. Home will then open Google Home.\n\nTo make Home open CleanFrame Sharp again, open CleanFrame → Settings → Home button and turn on Home interception again."</string>
    <string name="ui_8c04b97198e4" formatted="false">"Consumes Home press and release before normal Android Home handling, then opens CleanFrame once. No window watching, delayed retry or Google-launcher disable is used. Compatibility depends on TV firmware; verify on your device."</string>
    <string name="ui_dd17eb9d706e" formatted="false">"Android delivers global key events to the service. Only Home (3) is handled. All other keys pass through immediately without being stored. No screen contents, text, window events, gestures or touch exploration are requested."</string>
    <string name="ui_5736e7b7dbda" formatted="false">"First enable CleanFrame Home button in TV Accessibility, then turn on Home interception here. After an update, check the service is still enabled."</string>
    <string name="ui_907d447171f9" formatted="false">"Short and held Home presses both open CleanFrame once. The original long-press Home action is replaced while enabled. Voice, Back, volume, tuner and other keys are passed through. Screen-off and locked-device Home events follow the system path."</string>
    <string name="ui_4493721b67f9" formatted="false">"This Settings button pauses interception before opening Google Home. It stays paused until you turn it on again here."</string>
    <string name="ui_509146c051ee" formatted="false">"Pause Home interception here, or disable CleanFrame Home button in TV Accessibility. The original launcher remains enabled. Other Accessibility services are never changed by this app."</string>
    <string name="ui_61fa848397a2" formatted="false">"No network permission, screen retrieval or key history. Only the enable choice and a failure message are saved locally. The current service session shows whether a Home launch was requested; this does not prove the TV kept CleanFrame in front."</string>
    <string name="ui_bff680be0199" formatted="false">"Enable debugging using your TV manufacturer’s instructions. PC and TV must share the LAN. Open PowerShell in the folder containing adb.exe. Replace the example address and port below with your TV’s own values."</string>
    <string name="ui_9e1c8a552ab0" formatted="false">".\\adb.exe devices\nContinue only if it says device, not offline or unauthorized."</string>
    <string name="ui_d0003010be4c" formatted="false">".\\adb.exe shell pm list packages -d\nTest tuner, EPG, recording, HDMI, remote keys and streaming. If needed, restore the candidate and restart the TV. Never uninstall system packages or clear their data as recovery."</string>
